[SIZE="4"][B]About[/B][/SIZE]

This is an unofficial TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 build for the [B]LG L5 II E450g[/B] (codename [B]vee5ss[/B], MediaTek [B]MT6575[/B]). It uses a kernel built from LG's E450g source and is built from the Android 4.4 OmniROM/TWRP tree with the native 480x800 theme (portrait_hdpi, no scaling).

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only for the LG L5 II E450g. Do not flash it on the E450, E455, E460, E451g or the L4 II.[/B][/COLOR]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Requires root and the patched LK.[/B][/COLOR] The stock E450g bootloader refuses unsigned recovery images with a [I]Security Error[/I]. Follow this guide first:
[URL=""][GUIDE] How To Root and Unlock the Bootloader LG L5 II E450g (MT6575)[/URL]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status[/B][/SIZE]

Tested on real hardware, E450g with the patched LK:

[LIST]
[*]Boot to recovery, display and touchscreen
[*]ADB in recovery
[*]MTP (copy files from the PC while in recovery)
[*]Mount /system, /data and /cache
[*]External microSD (vfat), mounted and readable
[*]Install ZIP packages (used to install the CyanogenMod 10 ROM for this phone)
[*]Backup: Boot, System, Data, Cache, NVRAM, Logo, Uboot and Sec_RO, into a folder named after the model (TWRP/BACKUPS/LG-E450g)
[*]Reboot to System returns to Android (no recovery loop)
[/LIST]

[B]Not tested yet:[/B] a full backup-to-restore cycle. Do not rely on a TWRP backup as your only copy until someone confirms a restore.

[B]Not included:[/B] exFAT and decryption of an encrypted /data.

[SIZE="4"][B]Important notes[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Internal storage lives in /data/media.[/B] "Wipe > Factory Reset" and "Wipe Data" keep your internal storage (photos, downloads) by design. "Format Data" erases it.
[*][B]Do not rely on the NVRAM, Uboot and Sec_RO backup entries alone.[/B] They use MTK character devices and have not been verified with a restore. Back up your IMEI, NVRAM and calibration partitions with the [I]dd[/I] commands from Step 2 of the unlock guide as well, and keep them on your PC.
[*][B]Never format /persist_lg or /persist[/B] (mmcblk0p3 and mmcblk0p4). They hold LG factory and calibration data.
[*]There is no fastboot on this phone and "Reboot > Bootloader" is not offered: the LK has no fastboot mode.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[B]Before starting:[/B] the phone must be rooted and running the patched LK (see the guide above), with USB debugging enabled.

[B]1. Back up the current recovery:[/B]
[CODE]adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/recovery of=/sdcard/recovery-stock.img bs=512 count=14336; chmod 644 /sdcard/recovery-stock.img'"
adb pull /sdcard/recovery-stock.img[/CODE]

[B]2. Flash TWRP:[/B]
[CODE]adb push twrp-3.1.1-0.1-vee5ss.img /sdcard/twrp.img
adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/sdcard/twrp.img of=/dev/recovery bs=512; sync'"[/CODE]

[B]3. Verify the readback before rebooting:[/B]
[CODE]adb shell "su -c 'dd if=/dev/recovery of=/sdcard/twrp-readback.img bs=512 count=13816; chmod 644 /sdcard/twrp-readback.img'"
adb pull /sdcard/twrp-readback.img
md5sum twrp-readback.img
(Windows: certutil -hashfile twrp-readback.img MD5)[/CODE]
It must print [B]dfdc9a5e039081dae451da19d4829411[/B]. [COLOR="Red"][B]If it does not match, do NOT reboot:[/B][/COLOR] repeat Step 2.

[I]/dev/recovery[/I] is an MTK character device: always read it with [I]bs=512[/I] and an explicit [I]count[/I].

[SIZE="4"][B]Entering recovery[/B][/SIZE]

From Android or from TWRP:
[CODE]adb reboot recovery[/CODE]

With the phone off: press and hold [B]Vol+[/B], [B]Vol−[/B], the [B]center (Action) key[/B] and [B]Power[/B] together. When the LG logo appears, release Power and keep the other three held until TWRP loads.

